    "note": "Swept 2021-2026. The opening-range signal is real but roughly 0.019% per trade, against a 0.09-0.12% option cost hurdle. Longer holds do not help: the edge stops at the closing bell, and 3-5 day holds measured NEGATIVE. The book nonetheless holds overnight when src/live/hold.py prices the carry as worth it -- a deliberate choice against this finding, not a conclusion drawn from it. That gate uses the finding rather than ignoring it: overnight drift is taken as zero, so a hold has to be justified by geometry and paid for at a measured gap sigma. This book runs forward to gather out-of-sample evidence, not because it is expected to make money."
  }
